                <pb facs="0144" n="86" sameAs="frus:frus1866p3/pg86"/>


                <head>[Translation.]</head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Colonel Figueroa’s report.</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#center">STATE OF OAXACA—NORTHERN LINE—COLONEL-IN-CHIEF.</p>
                <p>At 6 o’clock this evening I occupied this town, after driving the enemy from
                    their formidable positions of Puente de Piedra, Puente de Tempascalapa, and
                    Cuesta del Limon—all strong places, regularly fortified.</p>
                <p>I shall take possession of Chuapam to-morrow. There is not a single soldier there
                    now; those that were left there have deserted.</p>
                <p>The traitor chief had the arms taken away; ten, however, remained on the
                    ground.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left">Independence and the republic!
                            <placeName>Villa-Alta</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1865-12-21">21st December, 1865</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>LUIS P. FIGUEROA.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The <hi rendition="#small-caps">General-in-chief <hi rendition="#italic">of
                                the Eastern Line, Tlacotalpan.</hi></hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
